    "body": "> The current implementation is aiming to identify any of the following common semantic-release placeholders:\r\n\r\nThat's perfectly fine I just wanted to make it more strict to prevent something like `1.4.21-foo-semantic-bar` being incorrectly matched. And yes, I'm not aware of anyone out there using such ridiculous prerelease identifiers but let's not underestimate people's creativity :stuck_out_tongue_winking_eye: \r\n\r\n",
